    "taskType": "task1",
    "text": "The bar chart compares the proportions of residents visiting a museum annually in North and South in 2010, 2015 and 2020. All figures are expressed as percentages.\n\nOverall, the proportion in North decreased overall, whereas South increased overall. South recorded the higher figure at the end of the period. The difference between the regions narrowed, from 45 percentage points in 2010 to 30 points in 2020.\n\nIn North, the figure stood at 71% in 2010, before falling to 51% five years later. It then declined to 31% in 2020. The first interval saw a change of 20 percentage points, while the corresponding movement during the second half of the decade was 20 points.\n\nSouth followed a different pattern, starting at 26% and reaching 41% in 2015. By 2020, its figure was 61%. Comparing the two regions directly, North had the larger share at the beginning, while South led at the end. The final figures of 31% for North and 61% for South therefore show a gap of 30 percentage points.",
